{
  "name": "The Tollhouse at Night",
  "intro": "Midnight at the old river tollhouse. Moonlight silvers the yard; a torch bobs along the fence line and another burns by the front door. Somewhere inside is Captain Morrow's ledger, the proof of who has been paying the river gangs. Nobody can know you were here.",
  "dmNotes": "Goal: take the ledger from the strongbox at P9 (Morrow keeps the key; picking the lock is a DC 15 thieves' tools ruling, 1 round; on a fail: noise P9 \"a sharp metallic clack\" --loud 40). Doors: front (F9/F10), back (R3/R4, locked: DC 13 to pick), store (storehouse to guardroom), office-w (storehouse to office), office (guardroom to office). Window win1 in the guardroom's north wall. The storehouse is pitch dark, the guardroom lamp-lit, the office lit only by Morrow's candle; the yard is moonlit (dim). Bram (torch) holds the front door facing south; Tilly (torch) walks the fence. Fang the mastiff sleeps by the yard path at K11: keen hearing and smell, wakes to noise. Sergeant Hask plays cards in the guardroom; he trusts Tilly more than Bram. Captain Morrow sits in the office, sees nothing directly, and commands through reports. All five are NPC minds: run \"minds\", \"tick\" between the players' moves out of combat, and \"mind <id> act\" on their turns in combat. If Morrow believes the ledger is threatened he takes it and heads for the back door.",
